---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Evidence · borck.consulting" pageClass="page" description="The public evidence behind borck.consulting: an applied local-AI lab, free tools, books, and teaching simulations.">

  <div class="hero">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">Evidence</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title">The method is public. The client work is private.</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      Most of what this practice knows is already visible. The lab, the tools, the books,
      and the teaching simulations can be inspected before a conversation starts. That is
      deliberate: judgment you can check is worth more than a brochure.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Inspect the work</span>
    </div>

    <div class="tier-grid">
      <a href="https://locolabo.org" class="tier-card" style="text-decoration:none;">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Applied research</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">LocoLabo</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          A personal research lab running local, privacy-first AI on secondhand hardware.
          Benchmarks, hardware bills of materials, and notes on what fails.
          This is the evidence behind the data-sovereignty work.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a href="https://trusttool.borck.education" class="tier-card" style="text-decoration:none;">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Free tool</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">The Trust Tool</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          A five-minute exercise that sorts AI tasks by consequence and precision.
          It shows where to trust the output and where a human has to stay in the loop.
          Use it before a Diagnostic to see how the judgment works.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a href="https://books.borck.education/conversation-not-delegation" class="tier-card" style="text-decoration:none;">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Framework</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Conversation, Not Delegation</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          The book that sets out the operating principle: AI assists, the human keeps
          the judgment. Free to download, CC BY 4.0, also on Amazon in Kindle and print.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a href="https://locoensayo.org" class="tier-card" style="text-decoration:none;">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Teaching simulation</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">CloudCore and the simulation lab</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          A simulated firm recovering from a data breach, with AI staff and a story that
          releases over a term. Taught across five units. The same rehearsal method can
          be adapted for a firm preparing for a real governance change.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Peer-reviewed research</span>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-sub" style="max-width: none;">
      The method has a theoretical basis. The paper explains why human complexity-management
      strategies improve LLM output, and where the transfer breaks down. It is conceptual
      research, not a study of consulting outcomes.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--gray-1); max-width: 600px;">
      Borck, M. (2026). <em>Cognitive Strategy Transfer: Why Human Complexity-Management
      Strategies Improve Large Language Model Performance</em>. Accepted at the
      Australasian Conference on Information Systems (ACIS 2026), Perth, Australia.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
      <a href="https://research.borck.dev/#cognitive-strategy-transfer" class="btn btn-secondary">Read the research</a>
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--gray-2); margin-top: 1rem;">
      This research was conducted in my academic role. The practice is independent and
      not endorsed by Curtin University.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Why this is public</span>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-sub" style="max-width: none;">
      The tools and books are free because the code is not the scarce part. Anyone can
      build a chatbot now. What is scarce is knowing which problem is worth solving,
      where the data may go, and when a human must sign off. Publishing the method keeps
      the practice honest and lets a buyer test the thinking before paying for it.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <a href="https://notes.borck.consulting" class="btn">Read the field notes</a>
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.9rem;">
      The method is published at
      <a href="https://notes.borck.consulting">notes.borck.consulting</a>, and the
      source is on
      <a href="https://github.com/michael-borck/local-ai-field-notes">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

</Base>
